{"id": "EUVD-2026-97681", "enisaUuid": "c80c5e7b-5331-301d-a999-6004c0202b6c", "description": "Crawl4AI from 0.9.0 before 0.9.4 contains an untrusted-config gate bypass that allows non-admin API clients to construct forbidden config objects by wrapping them in dict-type wrappers. Attackers can send a laundered LLMConfig with api_token set to an env reference via /config/dump to read SECRET_KEY and provider keys, enabling admin JWT forgery.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T02:27:16", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai/security/advisories/GHSA-5w5p-vcv6-mm3f", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/crawl4ai-0.9.0-before-0.9.4-untrusted-config-gate-bypass-leaks-environment-variables"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109237", "GHSA-r6v9-2q53-jfjp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.32, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac50483d-dc74-34a3-8d71-eba27ce8f698", "product": {"name": "Crawl4AI", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}, "product_version": "0.9.0 <0.9.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2915e52f-cdb4-3faa-84b4-60a924e80462", "vendor": {"name": "unclecode"}}], "isExploited": false}